theorem geometric-sum
  metamath    geoser
  let a ∈ ℝ                                                           (H1)
  assume a ≠ 1                                                        (H2)
  let n ∈ ℕ₀                                                          (H3)
  then G(n) = (1 − a^(n + 1))/(1 − a)

1.  1 − a ≠ 0
    algebra, from H2
    requires a ∈ ℝ: from H1

2.  G(n) = (1 − a^(n + 1))/(1 − a)
    induction on n starting at 0, from H3

    base
    2.1.  G(0) = 1
          def:stdlib/sums/G, from H1

    2.2.  a^(0 + 1) = a^1
          substitute 0 + 1 = 1 (arithmetic)

    2.3.  a^1 = a
          thm:stdlib/numbers/exponent-one a := a, from H1

    2.4.  a^(0 + 1) = a
          calculation
            a^(0 + 1) = a^1       2.2
                      = a         2.3

    2.5.  1 = (1 − a)/(1 − a)
          algebra
          requires 1 − a ≠ 0: from 1
          requires a ∈ ℝ: from H1

    2.6.  (1 − a)/(1 − a) = (1 − a^(0 + 1))/(1 − a)
          substitute a^(0 + 1) = a (line 2.4)

    2.7.  G(0) = (1 − a^(0 + 1))/(1 − a)
          calculation
            G(0) = 1                              2.1
                 = (1 − a)/(1 − a)                2.5
                 = (1 − a^(0 + 1))/(1 − a)        2.6

    step
    2.8.  For every k ∈ ℕ₀, if G(k) = (1 − a^(k + 1))/(1 − a)
          then G(k + 1) = (1 − a^((k + 1) + 1))/(1 − a).
          fix
          let k ∈ ℕ₀                                                  (K)
          assume G(k) = (1 − a^(k + 1))/(1 − a)                       (IH)

          2.8.1.  G(k + 1) = G(k) + a^(k + 1)
                  def:stdlib/sums/G n := k, from H1, K

          2.8.2.  G(k) + a^(k + 1) = (1 − a^(k + 1))/(1 − a) + a^(k + 1)
                  substitute G(k) = (1 − a^(k + 1))/(1 − a) (IH)

          2.8.3.  k + 1 ∈ ℕ₀
                  thm:stdlib/numbers/nat0-closure, from K

          2.8.4.  a^((k + 1) + 1) = a^(k + 1)·a
                  thm:stdlib/numbers/exponent-step m := k + 1, from H1, 2.8.3

          2.8.5.  (1 − a^(k + 1))/(1 − a) + a^(k + 1) = (1 − a^(k + 1)·a)/(1 − a)
                  algebra
                  requires 1 − a ≠ 0: from 1
                  requires a ∈ ℝ: from H1
                  requires a^(k + 1) ∈ ℝ: thm:stdlib/numbers/power-real m := k + 1, from H1, 2.8.3

          2.8.6.  (1 − a^(k + 1)·a)/(1 − a) = (1 − a^((k + 1) + 1))/(1 − a)
                  substitute a^((k + 1) + 1) = a^(k + 1)·a (line 2.8.4), right to left

          2.8.7.  G(k + 1) = (1 − a^((k + 1) + 1))/(1 − a)
                  calculation
                    G(k + 1) = G(k) + a^(k + 1)                         2.8.1
                             = (1 − a^(k + 1))/(1 − a) + a^(k + 1)      2.8.2
                             = (1 − a^(k + 1)·a)/(1 − a)               2.8.5
                             = (1 − a^((k + 1) + 1))/(1 − a)           2.8.6
